  "start_date_sort": "1243-12-31",
  "comments": "Van der Kuijp ([FEHIEFEB]: 143) lists as potential candidates: sKag pa ston gzhon (whom he discards as this contemporary of Sa skya Pa\u1e47\u1e0dita would have been too old), sBas pa ston gzhon (ID: 6651) (a possible option, although he is not explicitly associated with epistemology), and Cog ro ston gzhon (as the most likely option).\r\nUnderstood by Sun Weijin to be the \"'jam dbyangs ston gzhon\" in the Pram\u0101\u1e47av\u0101rttika lineage mentioned by 'Gos Lo ts\u0101 ba ([FEHIEFEB]: 143).\r\nHe traveled to the Mongol court in China in the early 1280s and translated in Tibetan Xuanzang's (ca. 602-64) Chinese version of \u015aa\u1e45karasv\u0101min's Ny\u0101yaprave\u015ba ([FEHIEFEB]: 165).\r\nA \"ston gzhon\" - maybe the same person - is also listed as the author of two works in the [8H6M69W4]:\r\n- Lam 'bras gyi bshad pa gsung ngag nyi ma'i 'od zer in 230 folios\r\n- Kun gyi sna lam du ma grags pa'i rin po che'i gsung 'ga' <gnyan ston tshul rgyal dang ston gzhon gnyis kyis> zin bris su mdzad pa rnams in 38 folios. ([FEHIEFEB]: 166).",
  "alternative_names": "ston pa gzhon nu\r\n'jam dbyangs ston gzhon",
  "external_links": "",
  "review": false,
  "start": "after 1200 before 1287",
  "end": "after 1297 before 1330",
